From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: knapcio <knapcio@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 10:08:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 26/30] K1: split table G6_K1_SPLIT (exact), translation
 prefetch G6_K1_TLBW, VMM weight image G6_IMG_VMM; k1_audit
 --tab/--alloc/--hold/--window/--tlb

bind.cuh: G6_K1_SPLIT="M:KS1xWG/NS2,..." (M or a-b, either part optional) per step row count for the trellis-shared
MoE layers. An fc1 shape is taken only where KS1 * WG equals the split's (same k range per partial, same fc2 sum
order); NS2 at any divisor of 384 (each z tile is one warp's sum over its block's 8 k-tiles). Same bytes by construction.
k1.cuh: G6_K1_TLBW=KB: fc1 CTA s prefetches one L2 line per granule of item slot s's fc1 + fc2 ranges at launch
start (separate, route-overlap part 2 and fused forms). No output change.
vmm.h + packfind.h rs_fill: G6_IMG_VMM=1|MB: the device image from cuMemCreate chunks mapped into one range
(driver API via cudaGetDriverEntryPointByVersion); DevImage::adopt takes a release function. Falls back to cudaMalloc.
k1_audit.cu: --tab (the k1 arm with a G6_K1_SPLIT table, checked == k1), tlbw arms,
--alloc each|one|vmm[:MB] (one = the engine's single allocation), --hold/--window (footprint vs allocation order),
pages touched per call at 4K/64K/2M, --tlb (pointer-chase translation probe + page size / THP / buddyinfo, read only).
